order event clue
1 {the schist forms (the oldest rock)} {cut by the granite}
2 {the granite pushes into the schist and cools} {cuts the schist}
3 {erosion wears the schist and granite flat} {the flat base of the sandstone}
4 {sandstone, limestone, shale and chalk are laid down} {one on top of the other}
5 {the layers are folded} {tilted, although laid down flat}
6 {the fault breaks the folded layers} {cuts all the layers}
7 {erosion carves today's hills; the river lays down its sand} {cuts everything}
